4    Optimization Algorithms
Five optimization approaches are employed to solve the formulated traffic-aware vehicle routing problem:
Quantum Particle Swarm Optimization (QPSO), classical Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO), Genetic
Algorithm (GA), Random Search (RS), and Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS).
All algorithms are evaluated using the same transportation instances,  traffic scenarios,  objective
function, constraint penalties, and maximum objective-evaluation budget.  This enables a controlled
comparison of their search performance.
5

4.1    Route Representation and Decoding
QPSO, PSO, GA, and Random Search employ a common random-key representation.  For a problem
containing N  customers, a candidate solution is represented by a continuous vector
x = (x
