The customer permutation is obtained by sorting the random keys:
π = argsort(x).(19)
The resulting permutation is subsequently decoded into vehicle routes using a greedy capacity-aware
splitting procedure.  The decoded routes are then evaluated using the common traffic-aware objective
function.
This representation allows continuous metaheuristic search methods to operate on the routing problem
while maintaining a common solution representation across multiple algorithms.
