10.3    Convergence
The evaluation-indexed convergence plots should be used to determine whether an algorithm:
1.  improves rapidly during early search;
2.  continues making meaningful progress late in the budget;
3.  converges prematurely; or
4.  exhibits high run-to-run variability.
